ffirm":0,"cut":1}],"ai_disruption":[0,0,0,0.0]},"move":{"r1":0.0287,"r5":0.0361,"r1_spy":0.0325,"r5_spy":0.0433}}],"quotes":[{"c":"WPC 2018 Q2","e":"wpc","d":"2018-08-03","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Brooks Gordon","x":"What's important to note is about half of that rent was shifted from properties that we've sold in a restructuring in 2009.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/08/06/w-p-carey-wpc-q2-2018-earnings-conference-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2018 Q2","e":"wpc","d":"2018-08-03","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Brooks Gordon","x":"So Agrokor is a tenant within CPA:17 that is going through restructuring.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/08/06/w-p-carey-wpc-q2-2018-earnings-conference-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2018 Q4","e":"wpc","d":"2019-02-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Brooks Gordon","x":"And we're presently working through restructuring leases with them kind of one by one, so nothing kind of material.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/22/w-p-carey-wpc-q4-2018-earnings-conference-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2018 Q4","e":"wpc","d":"2019-02-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"John Massocca","x":"But Universal Technical Institute, which was in the top 10 previously, has kind of talked about potentially restructuring how it views its real estate.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/22/w-p-carey-wpc-q4-2018-earnings-conference-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2019 Q1","e":"wpc","d":"2019-05-09","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Sheila McGrath","x":"And then just quickly on G&A, you maintain guidance for the year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/09/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q1-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2019 Q2","e":"wpc","d":"2019-08-02","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Toni Sanzone","x":"Most significant was the restructuring of the Agrokor portfolio, which comprises 23 grocery stores and one warehouse property acquired in our merger with CPA:17.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/02/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q2-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2019 Q2","e":"wpc","d":"2019-08-02","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Toni Sanzone","x":"Under the restructuring, we reached agreement with the tenant on new rents for 19 properties, increasing the ABR associated with those properties from $10.1 million to $15.4 million and extending their lease term to 15 years.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/02/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q2-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2019 Q3","e":"wpc","d":"2019-11-01","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Toni Sanzone","x":"And as a reminder, we expect to continue collecting pass through rents from this tenant in the same amount for the next two quarters.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/01/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q3-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2019 Q3","e":"wpc","d":"2019-11-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Toni Sanzone","x":"First, we collected $3.3 million in past-due rents as part of the restructuring of our Agrokor investments, which we discussed in detail on last quarter's call.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/01/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q3-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2019 Q3","e":"wpc","d":"2019-11-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Toni Sanzone","x":"Net income for the third quarter included a $26 million impairment charge to reduce the carrying value of a portfolio of four manufacturing facilities, which the tenant is currently working through corporate restructuring.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/01/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q3-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2019 Q4","e":"wpc","d":"2020-02-21","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Jason E. Fox","x":"Brexit has made some meaningful progress and fears of a trade war with China have eased somewhat.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/21/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2019 Q4","e":"wpc","d":"2020-02-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Toni Sanzone","x":"A portion of this related to the lease restructuring of four manufacturing facilities, which we discussed on our last earnings call.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/21/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2019 Q4","e":"wpc","d":"2020-02-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Toni Sanzone","x":"As anticipated, that restructuring included an initial rent reduction from $5.4 million to $1 million, but will steadily grow to $2.4 million by year four of the lease.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/21/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2020 Q1","e":"wpc","d":"2020-05-01","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Jason E. Fox","x":"The notable exceptions were fitness, theater and restaurants, which represent just 2% of our ABR, and for which we received only a very minimal amount of April rents.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/01/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2020 Q1","e":"wpc","d":"2020-05-01","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Jason E. Fox","x":"I think, Josh, it's also important to note that we mentioned that about 2% of our ABR only 2% of our ABR is in the part of the retail markets have been most impacted, fitness facilities, theaters and restaurants.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/01/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2020 Q1","e":"wpc","d":"2020-05-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jason E. Fox","x":"We expect this to be a small list, and we're very well positioned with critical assets, good collateral and a seasoned team with extensive restructuring experience.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/01/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2020 Q1","e":"wpc","d":"2020-05-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Toni Sanzone","x":"We have instituted a number of cost-savings measures since the start of the COVID-19 crisis, predominantly focused on discretionary spending.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/01/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2020 Q2","e":"wpc","d":"2020-07-31","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Jason E. Fox","x":"The minor exception to our strong portfolio performance continued to be fitness centers, theaters and restaurants for which we received 37% of second quarter rents, although these represent just 2% of our ABR.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/31/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2020 Q2","e":"wpc","d":"2020-07-31","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Toni Sanzone","x":"The other roughly 70% largely comprises rents due from our fitness center, moving theatres and restaurants and would only be recognized if collected.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/31/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2020 Q2","e":"wpc","d":"2020-07-31","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jason E. Fox","x":"This has afforded us considerable flexibility allowing us to opportunistically work with tenants on lease restructuring that create value.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/31/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2020 Q2","e":"wpc","d":"2020-07-31","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jason E. Fox","x":"During the second quarter, we entered into one such restructuring with a significant tenant.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/31/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WPC 2020 Q3","e":"wpc","d":"2020-10-30","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Toni Sanzone","x":"The remainder of the rent we did not recognize during the third quarter largely comprised rents due from fitness centers, theaters and restaurants, some of which have resumed paying reduced rent, but will remain on a cash basis for AFFO purposes for the foreseeable future.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/30/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WPC 2020 Q3","e":"wpc","d":"2020-10-30","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Brooks G. Gordon","x":"And then also the restructure of several theater leases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/30/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WPC 2020 Q3","e":"wpc","d":"2020-10-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jason E. Fox","x":"Of course, we're also -- I mentioned sale-leasebacks, we're also going to do our traditional sale-leasebacks, where timing of closing, complexity of the deal will also add to our pricing power.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/30/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WPC 2020 Q3","e":"wpc","d":"2020-10-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Toni Sanzone","x":"But it is something that we look at as we're kind of seeing positive pricing in the markets there.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/30/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WPC 2020 Q4","e":"wpc","d":"2021-02-12","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Toni Sanzone","x":"Second, and as expected, the bulk of our remaining uncollected rents are from tenants in the restaurant, fitness, and theaters category, which represented just 1.3% of the portfolio's ABR at year-end.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/12/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WPC 2020 Q4","e":"wpc","d":"2021-02-12","l":"t